# Copy to .env.local, or set these on your host.

# ---------- Database ----------
DATABASE_URL=postgres://gretlab:gretlab_dev_only@127.0.0.1:5433/gretlab

# ---------- Sign in (read when the site runs) ----------
# The site's public address. In development: http://localhost:3000
NEXTAUTH_URL=

# Signs the session cookie. Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=

# Google Cloud Console > APIs & Services > Credentials > OAuth client ID (Web application).
# Authorized redirect URI: <NEXTAUTH_URL>/api/auth/callback/google
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Comma-separated accounts that become admins on sign-in. Everyone else is managed in
# the dashboard. This is how the first admin exists.
ADMIN_EMAILS=

# Local development without Google. Ignored in production builds.
# AUTH_DEV_LOGIN=true

# Token for GET /api/metrics. Leave empty to keep metrics off.
# METRICS_TOKEN=

# Behind a connection pooler (PgBouncer, as serverless hosts need): turn off prepared
# statements, and keep each instance's own pool small.
# DATABASE_PREPARE=false
# DATABASE_POOL=10

# ---------- Lab exams limited to networks ----------
# Shared with Caddy so the app trusts visitors' addresses. At least 16 random characters:
# openssl rand -hex 24. Without it, exams can't be limited to a network (docs/deploy-exams.md).
# PROXY_SECRET=
# Or, on Vercel, nothing (its edge vouches). On another host, the header it puts the visitor's
# address in (cf-connecting-ip, x-nf-client-connection-ip, fly-client-ip). Only if visitors
# can't reach the app around that host (docs/deploy-exams.md).
# CLIENT_IP_HEADER=

# ---------- Optional features ----------
# Email notifications: smtp://user:password@host:587 (smtps:// for 465). Without it, in-app only.
# Queued and sent in batches with retries (features/notifications/outbox.ts). Either
# RESEND_API_KEY (Resend's API, batches of 100) or SMTP_URL (any mail server). MAIL_FROM must
# be on a domain the provider has verified.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# SMTP_URL=
# MAIL_FROM=GretLab <no-reply@your-college.edu>
# Lets a scheduler send big batches and retries: POST /api/cron/outbox with
# "Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>". At least 16 characters: openssl rand -hex 24
# CRON_SECRET=

# GitHub projects: a token raises GitHub's rate limit (60 lookups an hour without one) for
# pinning handed-in repositories to their commit. GITHUB_LOOKUP=off skips lookups (tests).
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_LOOKUP=off

# LTI 1.3: a fixed signing key (PEM, one line with \n for newlines) and its id. Without them a
# key is made on first use and kept in the database. LTI_ALLOW_HTTP=true lets LMS addresses be
# http, for local tests only.
# LTI_PRIVATE_KEY=
# LTI_KEY_ID=
# LTI_ALLOW_HTTP=true

# ---------- File storage (Cloudflare R2; README › File storage) ----------
# Images in problem statements and downloadable files (exports, import reports). Without
# these, everything stays in the database, as before. An API token with Object Read & Write on
# the two buckets only; neither bucket needs public access.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_PUBLIC_BUCKET=gretlab-public
# R2_PRIVATE_BUCKET=gretlab-private
# Optional: the public bucket's custom domain (needs the domain's DNS on Cloudflare). Without it,
# images are reached through links signed for 7 days.
# R2_PUBLIC_URL=https://files.gretlab.grettech.com
# Another S3-compatible store instead of R2 (the tests use S3Mock): its address.
# STORAGE_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9190

# ---------- Payments (Razorpay; Dashboard › Plans, README › Payments) ----------
# Organizations pay for their plans through Razorpay (UPI, cards, net banking). Without the keys,
# the plan page says paying online isn't set up, and plans are set by hand on Dashboard › Plans.
# Test keys (rzp_test_…) first; the key secret and webhook secret are secrets.
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
# The secret typed when adding the webhook (https://<site>/api/razorpay/webhook,
# events payment.captured and order.paid).
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# A stand-in Razorpay's address (the tests run one).
# RAZORPAY_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3197

# ---------- Judge machines from the dashboard (Dashboard › Judges; deploy/aws/README.md) ----------
# The AWS role the site signs in as through Vercel's OIDC (no AWS keys anywhere). Without it the
# Judges page says machines can't be started here.
# JUDGES_AWS_ROLE_ARN=arn:aws:iam::<account>:role/gretlab-web-judges

# ---------- Set by the host: don't set these yourself ----------
# NODE_ENV (production in builds), VERCEL=1 on Vercel (its edge's visitor address is trusted for
# lab exams), VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA (the commit judges are compared with, "Out of date").

# ---------- Tests only (e2e/run.sh sets them) ----------
# JUDGES_PROVIDER=fake            an in-memory AWS for the judges suite
# JUDGES_LATEST_VERSION=e2e-latest the commit judges count as current, instead of Vercel's
# RESEND_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3198 the fake email provider e2e/notifications.mjs runs
# WEBHOOKS_ALLOW_LOCAL=true        lets webhooks point at local addresses

# ---------- Ads (read at build time, so rebuild after changing) ----------
# With these empty the site runs with no ads and loads no ad scripts.

# From AdSense > Account > Account information, e.g. ca-pub-1234567890123456
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_CLIENT=

# From AdSense > Ads > By ad unit > Display ads. Each placement is off until its id is set.
# Create the sidebar unit as Fixed, 200 x 200. Create the other two as Responsive.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_SLOT_SIDEBAR=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_SLOT_PROBLEM_END=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_SLOT_PAGE_END=
